  "body": "### What is the issue with the HTML Standard?\n\nWhen `createImageBitmap` is called with `colorSpaceConversion:\"none\"`, the spec indicates [the following](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/imagebitmap-and-animations.html#dom-imagebitmapoptions-colorspaceconversion):\r\n\r\n>  * If val is \"none\", output must be decoded without performing any color space conversions. This means that the image decoding algorithm must ignore color profile metadata embedded in the source data as well as the display device color profile.\r\n\r\nIt would be helpful to to clarify that the result will be an `ImageBitmap` that has been stripped of its color space information, and is therefore treated like all other images that have no color profile metadata (see [here in canvas](https://html.spec.whatwg.org/multipage/canvas.html#colour-spaces-and-colour-correction) and [here in CSS color](https://drafts.csswg.org/css-color/#untagged)). In particular, the raw RGB color values from the source will be treated as though they are in the sRGB color space.\r\n\r\nMost likely this is best accomplished via an informative note, as is the case in the canvas section.",
